1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,667
Recurring work needs clear ownership, proof and timely follow-up. Google Sheets is the operating
interface.

2
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:13,333
This is the polished presentation workbook: four fictional employees, with daily, 7-day, 15-day and
30-day assignments.

3
00:00:13,333 --> 00:00:20,000
Its counts and due dates read actual backend state. The separate private QA environment appears later.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:28,333
Employees use Ops Tasks → My tasks. The sidebar shows assigned work, its due date and the required
proof.

5
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:36,667
Employee A is the project owner’s verified Google login. This daily task requires a report, not a Ticket
ID.

6
00:00:36,667 --> 00:00:45,000
The report records meaningful completed work, pending work and count, and blockers. This is fictional
demonstration work.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:53,333
The employee reports what was completed and what remains pending. Here, three fictional portal tasks
remain open.

8
00:00:53,333 --> 00:01:01,667
Blockers and optional remarks are recorded with the same submission. No second spreadsheet update is
required.

9
00:01:01,667 --> 00:01:10,000
Business time is simulated: 21 October at 16:00 India time. Authentication and execution time are real.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,500
Submit completion is clicked once. This is the genuine first presentation submission recorded for this
walkthrough.

11
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:25,000
Typing pauses and the backend wait are shortened by cuts. The following view shows the actual resulting
records.

12
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Daily 21 October is Completed. Its proof is recorded and the action source is AUTHENTICATED.

13
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,000
The other three employees retain separate assignments. No dummy employee is silently authenticated as
Employee A.

14
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Activity History contains exactly one completion event from that submission, with the verified employee
role.

15
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Business timestamp: 21 October. Actual execution: 13 October. The two clocks are deliberately distinct.

16
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Private Google identities remain in the private backend audit; presentation cells use stable role
aliases.

17
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:58,667
The administrator advanced only this presentation business clock to the next working day.

18
00:01:58,667 --> 00:02:05,333
Real n8n execution #143898 created one new daily cycle. Its business and actual execution timestamps are
visible.

19
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:12,000
A separate repeat, #143908, created zero. These executions are genuine retained results; no new run is
invoked here.

20
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Daily 22 October now appears Pending alongside the completed 21 October cycle.

21
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Daily work is generated independently each working day. Periodic tasks create linked next cycles on
completion.

22
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:31,333
The QA replay control repeats the already recorded 21 October submission; it does not complete the new
daily task.

23
00:02:31,333 --> 00:02:40,667
The actual sidebar response is “Duplicate prevented: existing completion retained”.

24
00:02:40,667 --> 00:02:50,000
Verified counts stay at 5 cycles, 1 Completed, 1 history event and 0 alerts. No extra completion was
created.

25
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Manager Review consolidates all four employees, overdue work and independent resolution status.

26
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:02,000
No presentation alerts have been run. Manager acknowledgement is demonstrated next using preserved
private QA evidence.

27
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:07,500
This new workbook has no alerts yet. Its empty log is not evidence of failed delivery.

28
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:13,000
Verified manager and leadership captures belong to the separate private QA environment. They are not
copied into this workbook.

29
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:20,333
We now transition to PRIVATE QA — TEST MODE: the separate environment used for the eight acceptance
scenarios.

30
00:03:20,333 --> 00:03:27,667
This corrected control page replaces the excluded earlier take. Private URLs and browser chrome are
removed.

31
00:03:27,667 --> 00:03:35,000
Business time is simulated; actual execution and capture times are real. Accepted records are preserved,
not reset.

32
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:43,333
The retained queue shows 8 cycles: 5 Completed and 3 Pending. Each employee has a distinct ID and
assignment.

33
00:03:43,333 --> 00:03:51,667
B, C and D have Ticket IDs and next cycles: 22 October, 30 October and 16 November respectively.

34
00:03:51,667 --> 00:04:00,000
Their completions are explicitly SIMULATED by the authorized administrator through the real engine. They
are not dummy Google logins.

35
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:08,000
This read-only evidence reader shows an earlier verified portal run, temporarily assigned to the owner
for authentication testing.

36
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Ticket QA-PORTAL7-001 closed the 13 October cycle, recorded one event and created 20 October
automatically. Final roles are unchanged.

37
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Six retained history events include five completions and one manager acknowledgement. Private actor
addresses are masked.

38
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Employee A’s daily reports are AUTHENTICATED. B/C/D completions are SIMULATED. The manager
acknowledgement is AUTHENTICATED.

39
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Notice the real execution timestamps beside simulated business time. One event is recorded per
successful state transition.

40
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:51,000
This is actual n8n execution #139398, inspected from its execution history, not newly run for recording.

41
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:59,000
At the business threshold of 17:15, two notifications flowed through claim, SMTP capture and receipt
recording.

42
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Green nodes and two-item branches show the completed orchestration. Private endpoint details are
redacted.

43
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Retained retry #139569 reserved zero notifications. Its SMTP branch did not execute.

44
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:19,000
The original two manager messages remain; normal workflow retries do not create another send.

45
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:27,333
This is the actual retained SMTP capture for Employee C, addressed to the safe manager test recipient.

46
00:05:27,333 --> 00:05:35,667
The message includes task, cycle, due time and pending-task reason. Business date is 15 October; capture
date is 13 October.

47
00:05:35,667 --> 00:05:44,000
Mailpit capture proves receipt by the test SMTP service. It does not establish external Gmail Inbox
delivery.

48
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Retained post-acknowledgement UI: the separate Google-authenticated manager reviewed Employee C.

49
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:54,000
The acknowledgement was recorded while the employee task remained Overdue / Pending. Private identity is
redacted.

50
00:05:54,000 --> 00:06:01,500
This previously recorded manager inspection shows C after its later, explicitly SIMULATED completion.

51
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:09,000
The acknowledgement remains, while proof and the next cycle appear independently. This is not a new
acknowledgement action.

52
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Actual retained leadership execution #139921 processed one message at the next-working-day 14:00
threshold.

53
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Employee D remained unresolved. Already acknowledged and completed Employee C was excluded. No new send
is triggered here.

54
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:37,333
The retained leadership message identifies Employee D, Portal Task C and its precise cycle.

55
00:06:37,333 --> 00:06:45,667
Reason: employee task unresolved. Actual capture was 13 October at 11:31:03.871 UTC; simulated business
time was 16 October at 14:00.

56
00:06:45,667 --> 00:06:54,000
This is Mailpit SMTP evidence. The safe logical leadership recipient is not a company or external
leadership mailbox.

57
00:06:54,000 --> 00:07:03,000
Alert_Log retains two manager messages and one leadership escalation for the final role scenario.

58
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:12,000
Transport and SENT state are recorded separately from task completion. Across preserved QA scenarios,
Mailpit captured 8 manager and 3 leadership messages.

59
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:18,000
This read-only report renders actual recorded outputs and execution IDs: manager 17:10 → 0; 17:15 → 2.

60
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Manager review target is next working day 10:00; leadership 10:00 → 0, 14:00 → 1. These are proposed
prototype policy times.

61
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Separate Friday/Monday-holiday testing rolled targets to Tuesday and skipped nonworking-day daily
recurrence.

62
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:37,500
Actual recorded manager and leadership retries reserved zero; daily recurrence created one cycle, then
zero on repeat.

63
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:45,000
Two overlapping administrator simulation calls for D created one completion and one next cycle. Two
distinct employee logins overlapping remain unverified.

64
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:51,000
This is previously recorded evidence from the separate receiving test Gmail account: the message carries
the Inbox label.

65
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:57,000
It is external Inbox verification, separate from Mailpit. No additional Gmail message is sent for this
walkthrough.

66
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:02,000
The retained second Inbox screenshot shows the other approved manager notification, also received at
10:09 AM.

67
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Only two controlled Gmail messages were sent. The main account was the sender; the separate test manager
was the recipient.

68
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:15,000
All eight integrated assignment cases passed against private QA. The 22 local checks are separate
supporting regressions.

69
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:23,000
The presentation deployment has its own narrower verified completion, recurrence, replay and
authorization checks. QA acceptance is not silently transferred to the copy.

70
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:27,000
A company deploys with its own Google accounts, credentials, recipients and access-separated employee
interfaces.

71
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:31,000
This shared workbook is an administrative/reviewer demo. Private QA stays private. The owner decides
whether to submit.
